# React → project skills

Before implementing React work, read and follow the matching skill under `.cursor/skills/`. Do not improvise past these skills when the subject matches.

| Subject | Skill path |
|---|---|
| Components, hooks, props, modular React structure, design → code | `.cursor/skills/react-components/SKILL.md` |
| Server state, fetching, caching, mutations, React Query / TanStack Query | `.cursor/skills/tanstack-query-best-practices/SKILL.md` |
| Tables, datagrids, sorting, filtering, pagination (`@tanstack/react-table`) | `.cursor/skills/tanstack-table/SKILL.md` |
| Zod schemas, `safeParse` / `parse`, `z.infer`, validation errors | `.cursor/skills/zod/SKILL.md` |
| UI/UX design: layout, color, typography, spacing, interaction patterns | `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md` |
| UI/UX review, accessibility audit, Web Interface Guidelines check | `.cursor/skills/web-design-guidelines/SKILL.md` |
| Refactor without behavior change (extract, rename, split, clean smells) | `.cursor/skills/refactor/SKILL.md` |

## How to apply

1. Identify the subject(s) from the task.
2. Read each matching `SKILL.md` (and linked rule files under that skill if present).
3. Follow that skill’s guidance for the change.
4. If multiple subjects apply (e.g. a form with Zod + Query), load all matching skills.
